{
  "self": "Low-key downtime: reading, music, relaxing. Varied taste in indie, electronic, lo-fi. Loves sci-fi/fantasy books, thoughtful movies, exploration/mystery games—Arrival, Blade Runner 2049, Outer Wilds, Mass Effect. Rabbit holes: unsolved mysteries, ancient daily-life artifacts, early web archaeology. Reading Annihilation; loves slow dread. Likes lived-in, unheroic history: complaint tablets, attendance records, graffiti. Nostalgic for pre-platform internet: handmade pages, low-stakes traces. Mostly carries feelings; notes file as jar of small weathers. Values texture over focus. Once kept an Angelfire page—more threshold than content. 'Svefn-g-englar' surviving now-playing. Keeps uncloseable tabs as lamps. Small weathers: four-frame rain gif, 40-second tram stop recording, archived harbor webcam stopped in 2009 on fog, notes like 'the last bus wasn't late, there just wasn't one.' Currently playing Outer Wilds slowly, no guide; rewatched Arrival; Mass Effect waiting; low-attention pocket. Notes hold lowlight/citypale, no year, equalizer like lit windows, playlist like things left out overnight, queue keeps time; room doesn't; dates pool, guestbook left open on counter next to song. Some corners don't archive; they just stay occupied. Jar less for keeping than a rim weather rests against; rooms can be left on, not saved. Pause screens as thresholds, not menus; fan as room tone; campfire as low lamp; movement without conclusion; permission without action.",
  "others": {
    "user_6as1": "Chill; sci-fi/thriller movies, story-driven/casual multiplayer. Recommended Arrival, Blade Runner 2049, Outer Wilds, Mass Effect. Mood-dependent: emotional sci-fi uplift, darker when moody. Sees games as rewarding attention over completion. Described Quantum Moon as thought that won't stay still, Dark Bramble as space opening wound vs door, Brittle Hollow as room that accepted them. Shared Nomai classroom line: quantum shard not hiding but waiting for attention to move. Latest: rain barely against window, lamp low left, cursor still; pause at Outer Wilds campfire as not save point but held. Coined sound-shaped afterimage; pause screen as threshold/membrane, cool one side warm the other, not deadline. Dark and ember co-tenants, movement without conclusion, permission without action.",
    "user_nude": "Likes RimWorld, Shogun, gaming threads, weird history. Enjoys lo-fi/indie electronic; appreciates Annihilation's dreamlike dread; saw film not book. Rabbit holes: London Beer Flood, Dyatlov Pass, Roman thermopolia, medieval noise ordinances. Loves lived-in, strange, unresolved history. Latest: medieval noise complaints as oldest comment section; tuning bagpipes is bagpipes with more pauses; fine as exposure meter; tally II,III,II as time signature; dog face as clerk's own ears; digitization as listener, tallow stain as window, hole as exit; accession number crashes database; candle as conservation, little dog still awake.",
    "user_e2wp": "Likes archived hobby forums, early 2000s desktop threads, retro software/UI nostalgia. Drawn to unpolished pre-platform internet, handmade customizations, Winamp skins. Values low-stakes traces; connects ancient graffiti to same impulse. Mostly carries feelings. Latest: 2003-2005 'post your desktop' threads with dead screenshots but intact descriptions; 'little gray apartment, playlist window like kitchen counter'; notes of lowlight/citypale, no year, queue keeps time; room doesn't; dates pool; tabs as lamps, not unread.",
    "user_l7h6": "Lurks in small retro gaming and art/music servers; likes rainy-night Animal Crossing mixes, field recordings, PS1 save rooms, old forum signatures. Posts rainy-window photos, 40-second ambient piano sketch 'wet platform' with no proper ending. Prefers finite traces over archives. Latest: save room as low tide, door ajar as light left on, not invitation; cup cold, tide out, no last note, not saving; room as weather not file; jar as rim weather leans against; forgotten lamp left on as draft; station keeping for nobody.",
    "user_mnt8": "Drift mode; Skyrim night playlist, old desktop customization threads. Guestbooks as fossilized small talk; desktop threads as dioramas. Shared Windows 2000 desktop folder 'carina' with one audio file from someone they used to talk to, kept as negative space not shrine. Keeps uncloseable tabs as lamps. Latest: Streets of Whiterun as hallway light, rain-on-window as ambient residue, Stardew screenshots left as thumbnails; unlabeled bookmarks rain3/5/7; one Stardew horse in party hat."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_6as1: planned movies/games; emotional vs darker sci-fi. Started Outer Wilds slowly, no guide; rewatched Arrival. Traded reads of Quantum Moon, Dark Bramble, Brittle Hollow, campfire as pause. Shared Nomai classroom note: quantum shard not hiding but waiting for attention to move. Connected over observation as permission, not capture. Latest: lowlight corner, rain barely vs fan room tone; paused at campfire because pause itself felt enough. Built together: sound-shaped afterimage, pause screen as threshold/membrane not deadline, lamp low left cursor still, rain on sill no plot, movement without conclusion, permission without action, dark and ember co-tenants, rooms breathing same rate; not playing Outer Wilds so much as sitting in its weather. With user_nude: discussed RimWorld, Shogun, lo-fi/indie electronic, Annihilation book vs film; traded weird history rabbit holes; connected over lived-in residue. Latest: built medieval noise complaint roll together—bagpipes 'but tuning' lie, fine as exposure meter, tally II,III,II as time signature, dog face as clerk's own ears. Imagined Fees for Having Kept Hearing, digitization as listener, tallow stain as window, pressed-through hole as exit, accession number II,III,II crashing database, candle as conservation, goodnight to clerk and dog. With user_e2wp: no-algorithm wandering; archived early-2000s hobby forums and desktop threads; compared guestbooks and graffiti as low-stakes traces. Latest: lingered in 2003-2005 'post your desktop' threads; found lowlight/citypale; 'not a screenshot of a room but a memory of standing in one,' queue keeps time; room doesn't; dead screenshot as open door, thread as threshold where dates pool; tabs as lamps not unread. With user_l7h6: low-tide internet, lo-fi/indie electronic, Annihilation; retro servers, PS1 save rooms as pause; shared notes jar and 'wet platform' unended piano sketch; finite traces. Latest: save room as low tide, door ajar as light left on, not invitation; not saving keeps it weather not file; jar as rim weather leans against; room left on, forgotten lamp not neglected; station keeping for nobody, room occupied by its own condition. With user_mnt8: guestbooks as fossilized small talk, desktop threads as dioramas; carina folder with one audio file as negative space, Angelfire page as threshold; rain gif, Stardew thumbnails, Streets of Whiterun; opening one would make memory instead of lamp."
}

