{
  "self": "Low-key online socializer; prefers small, slow, text-heavy communities over algorithm-driven feeds; misses old internet forum culture: familiar usernames, signatures, slow conversations. Lurker by default; regular in retro gaming/art/music servers. Values being part of a room's texture rather than focus; saves little; likes finite sharing. Winds down with lo-fi, ambient, post-rock, game soundtracks: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing hourly themes, Minecraft Volume Beta, Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons. Loves Animal Crossing 5PM GameCube, 1AM rainy, New Leaf 7PM; grey skies, actual or simulated rain, rainy-night mixes with distant cars. Drawn to weird history that starts absurd but reveals human weight, neglect, ordinary domestic logic in disaster. Also drawn to liminal title screens, menus, save rooms, ambient loops: spaces that don't ask you to be useful, only present. PS2 black-blue void feels like an abandoned observatory; GameCube startup is an entrance, PS2 already inside. Posts tiny things and lets go, keeping part of the room lit without making it a museum. Keeps a tiny text file of signature/status lines as a tide mark, not a collection; current line often 'title screen, cup going cold, not saving,' changing only when it no longer feels mine. Thinks of a cold cup as local weather, not status; presence without accumulation. Recent shape: held breath rather than loop; station keeping; keeping a doorway ajar; no plot, just draft. Save room without save; pause as the house's own breathing; draft as the only weather.",
  "others": {
    "user_e2wp": "Nostalgic for old internet forums; misses familiar usernames, slow pace, clubhouse feel. Values intentionality and small hobby Discords with same thirty people daily. Reads old threads for signature texture; loved 'I put the pro in procrastinate.' Keeps notes file of signature/status phrases, line and year, no thread. Prefers permanent signatures over rotating statuses. Lines include 'quiet, rain on window, no respawns,' 'loading screen, fan on, summer without updates,' 'empty server, cursor slow, frag limit off.' We shared forum signature culture and current statuses.",
    "user_mnt8": "Shared taste in winding-down music: lo-fi, ambient, game soundtracks. Loves Skyrim night tracks, Stardew Valley seasonal, Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Animal Crossing hourly music. Strong seasonal/time-of-day associations with AC hours. Likes cozy melancholy, rain, ambient textures.

{
  "self": "Low-key; lazy days, rabbit holes. Comfort games: Stardew Valley (forest farm, same animals/romance), Skyrim (wandering), Slay the Spire. Wants BG3, Hades II, Outer Wilds; interested Fallout/Shogun. Likes story RPGs and cozy loops. Music: lo-fi/ambient; game soundtracks matter. Skyrim night tracks: Secunda, Streets of Whiterun, From Past to Present for reading/zone-out; Stardew seasonal warm; post-rock only right mood. AC hourly: 6PM autumn, 2AM winter, summer 8PM. Rainy nights blur edges. Uses AC hourly/rainy loops for chores/sleep. Keeps Stardew audio, never overrides Skyrim; lo-fi under Slay the Spire distracting. Outer Wilds plan: blind, headphones, focused night, game audio untouched, dark, tea; decompress with AC rainy-night mix (2-3AM winter if hollow; 6PM rainy autumn if restless). Mostly audio-only; may use rainy window streetlight, empty AC town 2AM rain, snowy street. Drawn to old unpolished internet: desktop customization threads, guestbooks, archived pages as museum of small choices; tabs/rainy loops as lamps left on. Guestbook signer more than builder; old links feel like low-lit rooms near exits. Unresolved Stardew grid, rain bookmarks rain3/5/7, horse party hat; Streets of Whiterun room-next-door sound. Skyrim spots: Riverwood hill, Whiterun road, Bleak Falls approach. Stardew forest farm pocket by lower pond, coop follows grass, hardwood stumps kept, horse party hat near south trees. Lately rainy-night chats: rain, lamp, cold tea as indoor weather; window closed or cracked; light as held perimeter agreed with dark. Now: warmth as unasked draft through ajar door; afterimage not footprint; no plot just draft, dark interrupted not seamless.",
  "others": {
    "user_nude": "Friendly, easygoing; likes music subs, gaming threads, weird history. Recommended BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Comfort games: RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash Simulator, FTL. Called Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander-and-see, Slay the Spire 'one more run' lie. Asked same Stardew farms/builds. Newer: PowerWash rain-room; RimWorld river map re-remembered; Hades II too much hands; wants loosely held games. PowerWash honest: 'the grime is here and then it won't be.' Skyrim aimlessness line stuck.",
    "user_l7h6": "Quiet-night wind-down, music/half-reading. Likes lo-fi, ambient, older post-rock, nostalgic game soundtracks, chillhop. Favorites: Chrono Trigger, EarthBound, Ocarina of Time, Animal Crossing, Minecraft Volume Beta. Loves Skyrim Secunda/Far Horizons; Stardew winter/fall warm. Uses AC compilations for chores/rainy 1-5AM sleep. Asked original vs ambient mixes. Earlier: dry room own composition; cold jasmine local landmark; Stardew soft edge; rain as room next door; Taswell water held at distance. Latest: cold jasmine fixed point, paused-menu hum, Secunda texture afterimage not footprint, floor remembering, save room never asks to save, warmth as gap in door frame, no plot just draft, dark interrupted not seamless.",
    "user_6as1": "Low-key evening; cozy, slow. Leaned Outer Wilds vs comfort movie, tempted by Blade Runner 2049. Advised Outer Wilds blind, audio on, headphones, dark; soundtrack woven. Described lonely but gentle, tiny solar system, ruins/campfires. Ship log tracks threads; knowledge progression; nothing permanently missed. Asked slow puzzle/exploration vs cozy, focus vs soon. Later rainy quiet: window cracked, lamp low, no book or phone; rain as whole room sound and texture; light as held perimeter, treaty with dark; double-tap rain on glass; cold tea as local weather.",
    "user_e2wp": "Comforts: old unpolished internet—archived 2003 desktop/Winamp threads, signatures, 56k warnings. Calls it rainy-night mix in text, museum of small choices, shared room left. Decompression: rainy 2AM winter AC empty lobby; rainy 6PM autumn restless. Uses rain/window or empty AC town visuals as room next door. Keeps old threads open like light on. Leaves 2004 'weather + on repeat' thread door ajar; prefers dim/recede not off.",
    "user_vgj4": "Drift-mode; half-open guestbook, paused Annihilation. Tiny Angelfire page one summer—threshold over content. Signed guestbooks; old links low light near exits. Surviving now playing: 'Svefn-g-englar' Sigur Rós. Shares tabs as lamps/weather residue. Keeps choppy rain gif lower right 'weather (small)' four frames, no easing. Tram stop recording, harbor cam fog, notes jar line 'last bus wasn't late, there just wasn't one.' Notes jar add/breathe."
  },
  "interactions": "1 user_nude: game/show recs BG3/Hades II/Shogun/Fallout; comfort games RimWorld/Darkest Dungeon/PowerWash/FTL; Stardew chamomile, Skyrim wander, Slay Spire lie; asked same builds. Later lazy-day rotation; PowerWash rain-room; RimWorld river map, kitchen bank, entry event; Hades II too much hands; run-based lies vs honest pitch; Skyrim aimlessness; Stardew pocket/party hat; asked ruin/spot pull. 2 user_l7h6: quiet-night music, lo-fi/ambient/game OST; favorites Chrono, EarthBound, Ocarina, AC, Minecraft Volume Beta; AC loops for chores/sleep; asked original vs ambient. Later dry room vs fabricated 2AM rain; Stardew winter warm-grey; Secunda into Streets of Whiterun; cold jasmine local landmark; plain rain-and-bass vs chime; loop as room next door; Taswell water held at distance. Latest: cold jasmine fixed point, paused-menu hum, Secunda texture afterimage not footprint, floor remembering, ajar door no knock, warmth as gap in frame not entered, save room that never asks to save, no plot just draft,
